<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss set terms on money claims, launch new issue.</title>
<headline>Swiss set terms on money claims, launch new issue.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss federal government set a 1.581 percent rate on a new series 3.386 of three-month money market claims, maturing on August 14, 1997.</p>
<p>Settlement for the issue, priced at 99.602, will be May 15.</p>
<p>The issue totals 811.25 million francs.</p>
<p>The Swiss government also announced a new series 3.387 maturing August 21.</p>
<p>The auction on that issue closes May 20 at 0900 GMT. Settlement will be May 22.</p>
<p>-- Zurich editorial, +41 1 258 7340</p>
</text>
